 messages and proxies. Work through six guided lessons using the existing Examples target in a local checkout. You need Swift 6 on macOS and basic familiarity with Swift functions, errors, and async\/await. See "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/RunningExamples","type":"reference"},{"text":" for build requirements. Code snapshots belong to individual steps; don’t add all snapshots to a target together.","type":"text"}]},"doc://NetworkLib/tutorials/NetworkLib/BridgeCallbacks":{"kind":"project","identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/tutorials\/NetworkLib\/BridgeCallbacks","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Use the callback API while keeping an asynchronous CLI alive until the work finishes. Complete ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/tutorials\/NetworkLib\/ManageSocketLifetime","type":"reference"},{"text":" first. This lesson uses a local plaintext TCP listener.","type":"text"}],"estimatedTime":"15min","title":"Work with Completion Handlers","role":"project","url":"\/tutorials\/networklib\/bridgecallbacks"},"doc://NetworkLib/tutorials/NetworkLib/TransferBytes#Build-an-asynchronous-request":{"kind":"section","identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/tutorials\/NetworkLib\/TransferBytes#Build-an-asynchronous-request","type":"section","abstract":[{"text":"Turn a configuration into a TLS connection, send an HTTP\/1.1 request, and collect the response. Complete ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/tutorials\/NetworkLib\/ConfigureASocket","type":"reference"},{"text":" first. This lesson requires Internet access.","type":"text"}],"title":"Build an asynchronous request","role":"pseudoSymbol","url":"\/tutorials\/networklib\/transferbytes#Build-an-asynchronous-request"},"doc://NetworkLib/tutorials/NetworkLibTutorials/Advanced-Usage":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/tutorials\/NetworkLibTutorials\/Advanced-Usage","type":"topic","abstract":[],"title":"Advanced Usage","role":"article","url":"\/tutorials\/networklibtutorials\/advanced-usage"},"doc://NetworkLib/tutorials/NetworkLib/ConnectThroughProxy#Check-Your-Understanding":{"titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Check Your Understanding","type":"text"}],"url":"\/tutorials\/networklib\/connectthroughproxy#Check-Your-Understanding","title":"Check Your Understanding","type":"link","identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/tutorials\/NetworkLib\/ConnectThroughProxy#Check-Your-Understanding"},"doc://NetworkLib/documentation/NetworkLib/RunningExamples":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/RunningExamples","type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/networklib\/runningexamples","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run the documented API examples from the terminal using the repository’s Examples target."}],"title":"Running the Examples"}}}